WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.279
Film Courage: We talked earlier about the anxiety of
this [entertainment] business. Can we talk about why it's

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:11.759
high anxiety and what can people do to
work with it? Jason Satterlund, Filmmaker: Most people I know in this

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:17.369
business is full of anxiety I mean first
of all if you most people in film don't

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:21.900
have full-time jobs most people you know
it goes like this

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.750
so there's this financial anxiety first
of all you know have busy seasons spring

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:32.730
summer and fall are often really busy
winter is usually not so sometimes

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:37.140
you're like I don't know I don't know
how to pay my rent next month that's

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:42.750
very common unless you're working making
gobs of money you're probably fine but

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:48.320
so that's the first off second of all is
we've all sacrificed so much to be here

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.309
nobody wants to make bad stuff so when
you get these opportunities you want to

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:58.890
do a good job and you can end up putting
so much pressure on yourself that you

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:03.629
start screwing things up that that's the
hall man sometimes there's anxiety for

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.869
the people that you're working with you
know you get a name talent for example

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:10.290
an a-lister actor that's coming in and
you're so afraid

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:15.780
I think it's afraid of being discovered
as a fake or you know not talented or

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.200
whatever your worst possible fear may be
you don't have it and the actor can see

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:25.740
it no no you know what happen oh man
yeah anxiety there there's the judgments

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.909
the egos you know someone thinking
they're more than they are and they're

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:35.009
just their ego is ruling the set and the
anxiety that comes out of that you're

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:39.150
also on film you know it's such a
collaborative art all these

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:42.810
temperamental artists in a room together
on set you know sets or pressure cookers

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.750
we're all working in under tight
deadlines and tight financial

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:50.430
restrictions the Sun is going down we
got to get the shot that's all super

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:54.329
anxiety so it's something I've
definitely struggled with most of my

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:57.750
life
I can be very high-strung and it's

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:03.270
something I really have to pay attention
to because I anxiety is a killer you

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:07.819
know it can give you health problems it
can it will shut down your creativity

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:12.109
you can
work yourself into such a state where

00:02:12.109 --> 00:02:19.819
you can get panic attacks and things
I've had that happen like yeah it's so I

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:23.719
think it's important first of all you
know I practice a lot of you know

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:27.200
self-awareness and meditation and things
like that just to help me deal with a

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.709
lot of those issues and you know not
that's a big rabbit hole but I will tell

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:33.739
you that one thing that's helped me a
lot is there are two ways to look at

00:02:33.739 --> 00:02:38.989
anxiety so your mind is like this
freeway cars racing back and forth on it

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:45.260
and you know money's flying out the door
oh this actors coming I'm so scared you

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.019
know it's going back and forth well you
got a couple of options you can either

00:02:48.019 --> 00:02:52.730
stand in the middle of traffic and try
to slow the cars down and stop being so

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:57.829
anxious and fight it or you can sit on
the overpass while the traffic's going

00:02:57.829 --> 00:03:04.150
under you and go okay there's a lot of
anxiety happening right now okay and

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:10.780
don't judge it and let it be and just
acknowledge that it's there and

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:17.750
sometimes it'll start to move away you
know you're not trying to stop the

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.310
traffic you're not trying to be angry at
the traffic because that doesn't help

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.329
you're not trying to you know you're
just acknowledging that it exists

00:03:26.329 --> 00:03:29.989
without any judgment and I also think
it's important to not say I try to avoid

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:35.930
the words I am anxious it's the same way
of saying I am depressed well I am NOT

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:42.829
the emotion of anxiety I am Jason a
person with strengths and weaknesses I

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:50.720
am NOT anxiety I am NOT anxious I am
feeling this way right now but not I did

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.959
because we I think we all have a
tendency to do that I am a pessimist

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:58.759
well you're right you're right you're
labeling yourself with a certain emotion

00:03:58.759 --> 00:04:02.090
and that can I think that can carry a
weight so I think those kinds of

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.139
self-awareness techniques are really
important especially for filmmakers who

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:12.680
are in such a high-stress industry and
you know taking time to laugh at

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.419
yourself and realize how silly this
business is sometimes and like I was

00:04:17.419 --> 00:04:21.150
shooting a thing earlier this year that
it was the feature I just did what

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:25.360
we had to shoot some anti-gravity stuff
and we had the camera on a thing called

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.590
a lambda head so you go left and right
and it's very much like Star Trek where

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:32.590
they you know they're all the actors had
to throw themselves one direction while

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:36.160
we rolled the camera the other way and
so in the monitor it looks like

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.510
everything's tilting and the actors are
going whoa

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:45.400
and I'm you know it's an intense scene
and I'm looking at it and I just start

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:51.070
laughing because it house
silly it all is like how silly this

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:56.919
whole make-believe industry is like and
I think that's healthy you know to like

00:04:56.919 --> 00:05:01.360
oh my goodness look over mate this is so
dumb what we're doing and so funny and

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.110
fun and all of that all together just
laughing at yourself for a minute you

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:09.130
know and just you know letting some of
that anxiety go and just because it's

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:12.190
not helping it's not serving you know
it's not making you more creative it's

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:17.430
not making you more meticulous or
anything it's just making you anxious

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:22.060
yeah another thing too is that the
decisions change very quickly in this

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.840
industry in so many ways and all of a
sudden like oh you know I'm so sorry we

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.400
don't need you and you don't know why
you'll never be told why so knowing that

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.050
that could happen and to not even though
you really want something but to know

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:39.430
that you could get that email or that
phone call really sorry yeah it's not

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:44.050
gonna happen happens all the time and
and to just alright be depressed for

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:51.450
like a day and then move on yeah I think
it's important to say that it's anxiety

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.940
especially when it results from things
like that or depression or

00:05:54.940 --> 00:06:00.220
discouragement it's okay it's okay to be
a little frustrated when you get the

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:05.050
rejection that's all right don't dwell
on it let yourself feel it and then you

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:10.120
know give yourself a day or two and then
try to move past it like but don't judge

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:14.200
the fact that you're just a little bit
down because you entered the festival

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:20.169
that you wanted and they didn't just
accept you yeah it sucks we all do it

00:06:20.169 --> 00:06:23.620
we're not no one's different
no one's different we're all the same

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:28.539
and it just it's okay to feel that way
but then just give yourself a chance to

00:06:28.539 --> 00:06:34.970
take a breath fight again another day
because it is normal this business is so

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:39.200
uncertain you know how many investors
I've talked to over the years trying to

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:44.570
get a movie out oh man the amount of
times they pulled out it's maddening

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:51.050
sometimes close to the shooting date oh
sure yeah that's all the DPS pull out

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:56.030
actors pull out projects fall apart and
that's that ranges from feature films to

00:06:56.030 --> 00:07:01.970
any any a manner of film job you know
shoot I had a I had like three or four

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:08.780
weeks of work booked on on 2001
September 11 you know I was let's go to

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.810
Egypt for a couple of weeks on a nice
great big fat job and I was gonna leave

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:17.270
on September 14 and I watched those
Towers fall and my work stopped dead

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:25.040
that was depressing that was hard but
normal what happens this is the business

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:31.880
that we fought to be in so you know try
to enjoy it as often as you can because

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.700
it's fun what a night when it's working
it's great sure it's great

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:44.629
you

